midwire-web-ui (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Captures: a "Delete all" button. It asks once more first, and keeps the
    capture that is being written.
  * The warning about being connected through the USB-C cable no longer
    assumes the link's interface is called midwire0. It reads the name from
    midwire-base, which is fixed in 0.4.1 to bring the link up properly.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

midwire-web-ui (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Network tab: switch for the network link over the USB-C cable that
    midwire-base 0.4.0 provides while the proxy is idle.
  * Proxy tab: warn before starting the proxy when the page itself is
    reached over that cable, since starting takes the port.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000

midwire-web-ui (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Setup wizard after login while the admin password or the Wi-Fi
    hotspot's password is still the factory default, with a reminder on
    the page for whatever is skipped.
  * Settings: turn SSH on or off, set a system user's password (creating
    the user on a device that has none) and manage that user's SSH keys.
    Passwords and keys are refused while the admin password is the default
    or empty. The work is done by the helper in midwire-base 0.3.0.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000

midwire-web-ui (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Updates tab: shows installed and available versions of Midwire's
    packages, checks for updates and installs them, with live progress.
    The work is done by the updater in the midwire-base package.
  * Auto-start: a device that has a network interface is started once it
    has been started from the page before. Previously it was always
    skipped, without saying so.
  * Auto-start: say on the Proxy page why an arriving device was not
    started, and log the decision.
  * Auto-start: notice a device that is pulled and pushed back in within
    a second.
  * Only warn that proxying a device cuts off the page when the page is
    in fact reached through that device. Ignore interfaces that are down.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000

midwire-web-ui (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: device list, start and stop with per-device options,
    live log, captures, saved settings with auto-start, Wi-Fi hotspot and
    client settings, admin login.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
